WP18 no-claim proof:

- Inventory evidence is not treated as use: no inventory runtime rows are
  counted by the new contract.
- Runtime evidence is not foreground: the contract requires an explicit
  duration source and does not infer foreground from running duration.
- Foreground evidence is not content: no content, title, or screen text fields
  are introduced.
- Launcher evidence is not game proof: launcher-only rows are excluded by
  contract.
- Launcher-game candidates are not known games: they count only under
  include-parent-approved-candidates with parentAllowedCandidate=true.
- Rating, UGC, multiplayer, and purchase signals cannot enforce directly: the
  signal schema rejects direct-enforcement for those signal kinds.
- Dry-run cannot execute: decisions require dryRun=true and handoff state is
  limited to not-requested/manual-required.
- Manual-required cannot execute: this slice does not call adapters or create
  dispatch-ready action results.
